      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To solve the problem \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute the value of \\(x\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression step by step.\n3. Write the final solution in \\boxed{}.\n\nStep 1: Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\((2x + 5)^2\\).\n\n\\[\n(2(3) + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nStep 2: Simplify the expression inside the parentheses first.\n\n\\[\n2(3) = 6\n\\]\n\nSo the expression becomes:\n\n\\[\n(6 + 5)^2\n\\]\n\nStep 3: Add the numbers inside the parentheses.\n\n\\[\n6 + 5 = 11\n\\]\n\nNow the expression is:\n\n\\[\n11^2\n\\]\n\nStep 4: Calculate the square of 11.\n\n\\[\n11^2 = 11 \\times 11 = 121\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\((2x + 5)^2\\) when \\(x = 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{121}\\).",
